  "title": "The three 4-flows conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every graph $G$ with no bridge, there exist three disjoint sets $A_1,A_2,A_3 \\subseteq E(G)$ with $A_1 \\cup A_2 \\cup A_3 = E(G)$ so that $G \\setminus A_i$ has a nowhere-zero 4-flow for $1 \\le i \\le 3$.",
